1. In what way are React components meant to be "pure functions"
   Functions that always return the same value when input with the same variables


2. What is a "side effect" in React? What are some examples?
   Any code that affects or interacts with an outside system(API calls etc.)



3. What is NOT a "side effect" in React? Examples?
   Anything that React is in charge of.


4. When does React run your useEffect function? When does it NOT run
   the effect function?
   On initial render, and whenever the dependencies array value has changed between renders


5. How would you explain what the "dependecies array" is?
   An array which value is compared between the previous render and current render, to determine whether the useEffect function runs again
